    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">30 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Structural pattern</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Tier 3: recognise and explain</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Bridge</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Stop a class hierarchy from multiplying when two things vary at once. Split \"what\" from \"how\", join them with one reference, and see that the Linux VFS with <code>file_operations</code> has been doing exactly this since long before you read about patterns.</p>\n"
